<div class="row"><div><label>Smell of gas?</label><select id="ttsmell"><option value="n">No</option><option value="y">Yes</option></select></div><div><label>Pipework-only retest</label><select id="ttretest"><option value="x">Not done yet</option><option value="ok">No perceptible movement</option><option value="bad">Perceptible movement</option></select></div></div>
<div id="ttres"><div class="v ok">Permissible drop for this IV: <b>8 mbar</b><br>PASS: no perceptible movement and no smell of gas. Now test disturbed joints, and pipework between each appliance and its isolation valve, with LDF.</div></div><button class="btn" id="ttcp">Add result to CP12</button><p id="ttcpmsg" class="note"></p>
<p class="note">Test at 20–21 mbar (natural gas) after a 7–10 mbar let-by test and 1 minute stabilising, then a 2-minute test. Edition 4 is mandatory from 1 October 2026. Permissible drops, perceptible-movement limits, retest rules and purge volume match Gas Safe Industry Standard Update 133 (Ed. 2, 15 April 2026). Test pressures and pipe and meter volumes come from published guides, not that document, so check them against IGEM/UP/1B Ed. 4.</p></div>
<div class="card"><b>3. Pipe sizing for gas flow (BS 6891:2015 Annex A)</b>
<p class="note">Add each section of pipework on the path from the meter outlet to one appliance. A section carries the combined load of every appliance beyond it. Check each appliance path separately.</p>
<div class="row"><div><label>Gas</label><select id="psg"><option value="ng">Natural gas (limit 1 mbar)</option><option value="lpg">LPG propane (limit 2 mbar)</option></select></div><div><label>Pipe material</label><select id="psm"><option value="cu">Copper</option><option value="st">Steel</option></select></div></div>
<div id="psr"><div class="card" style="background:var(--bg)"><b>Section 1</b><button class="btn alt" style="width:auto;padding:4px 10px;margin:0;float:right" data-pd="0">✕</button><div class="row"><div><label>Net kW carried</label><input data-p="0" data-k="kw" type="number" inputmode="decimal" value="24"></div><div><label>Pipe size (mm)</label><select data-p="0" data-k="s"><option value="0">8</option><option value="1">10</option><option value="2">12</option><option value="3">15</option><option value="4" selected="">22</option><option value="5">28</option><option value="6">35</option></select></div><div><label>Length (m)</label><input data-p="0" data-k="L" type="number" inputmode="decimal" value="6"></div></div><div class="cpg" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)"><div><label style="font-size:.7rem">Elbows 90°</label><input data-p="0" data-f="0" type="number" inputmode="numeric" value="2"></div><div><label style="font-size:.7rem">Bends 90°</label><input data-p="0" data-f="1" type="number" inputmode="numeric" value="0"></div><div><label style="font-size:.7rem">Bends 45°</label><input data-p="0" data-f="2" type="number" inputmode="numeric" value="0"></div><div><label style="font-size:.7rem">Tee in</label><input data-p="0" data-f="3" type="number" inputmode="numeric" value="0"></div><div><label style="font-size:.7rem">Tee out</label><input data-p="0" data-f="4" type="number" inputmode="numeric" value="0"></div><div><label style="font-size:.7rem">Other allowance (m)</label><input data-p="0" data-f="5" type="number" inputmode="numeric" value="0"></div></div></div></div><button class="btn alt" id="psadd">+ Add section</button><button class="btn alt" id="pssug">Suggest sizes</button>
<div id="psres"><div class="v ok">Total loss 0.41 mbar against a 1 mbar limit: PASS</div><div style="overflow-x:auto"><table style="margin-top:8px"><tbody><tr><th>#</th><th>Flow m³/h</th><th>mbar/m</th><th>Adj. m</th><th>mbar</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2.44 → 2.5</td><td>0.0565</td><td>7.2</td><td>0.41</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
<p class="note">Method: net kW × 1.1 gives gross, converted to flow (38.9 MJ/m³ natural gas, 93.1 MJ/m³ LPG). Flow is rounded up to the next tabulated rate, then loss per metre × (length + fitting allowances from Table A.5). Each section loss is rounded up to 2 decimals as in the standard’s example. Loss per metre is calculated with the Annex A formula and matches Tables A.1–A.4 within 0.4% (checked against the standard’s worked example). Annex A is informative: get accurate loss data from the pipe maker, and add fittings such as regulators and flexible connections from their data. The fitting allowance uses the largest connection size on the fitting, which can be bigger than the section: enter any difference under Other allowance. Up to 35mm only.</p></div>
</section>
</main>

</body></html>
